  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 589a77387c7c4ea488d9368fe6c3cd2f, type: 3}
  m_Name: Subgoal Dialogue 2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  characterName: Axion
  dialogues:
  - Now that you have made the EMBEDDING, only one step is left in building the POSITIONAL
    ENCODER...
  - The EMBEDDING you created contains syntactic information about the RESOURCES,
    representing each item in its own way. However, it doesn't contain any information
    about the relation between these items. A set of nails might be used to make
    a table, but when paired next to a circuit board and plastic it becomes clearer
    what the end product should be.
  - To facilitate the understanding of the relationship between each RESOURCE in
    the EMBEDDING, we should add some additional information about the position of
    each item in the sequence.
  - By using a mixture of a sine and cosine function, we can create unique offsets
    for each item in the EMBEDDING. These offsets can just be added onto our existing
    EMBEDDING.
  - Pass your newly created EMBEDDING into the POSITIONAL FACTORY to add positional
    information to the embedding.
